MID_SE_Pet_Max_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_001: It's Jester! He's so scary. I better take a detour.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_002: Huh? Hey, wasn't that...
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_003: Really flew off there! Trying to escape, huh?
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_004: Wh-wh-why are you chasing me?!
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_005: Heh heh HEH! See, I found myself a little plaything.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_006: Is that my handkerchief? Did you pick it up for me?\n'Cause it's not a plaything, ya know.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_007: So innocent! Don't you know anything about me?\nI'm always looking for new victims.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_008: Wittle bunny dwopped his hanky for me to pick up...
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_009: So I'm gonna have fun with YOU!
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_010: Ngh... I knew you were scary!
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_011: Come on, take it! I'm not exactly known to be\npatient...or peaceful.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_012: Eep...
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_013: Uh... Was I really that scary?
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_014: Y-yes. Very. You still are.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_015: Sorry, I guess I overdid it. Though I guess it's good to\nknow I can cause fear like that.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_016: D-do you enjoy threatening people?
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_017: No, I don't, actually. There's a lot going on, and—\nI sort of have to.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_018: I'm playing Jester to hide my identity. It wouldn't be\nconvincing if I didn't commit to it.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_019: So all that just now... That was just acting? You must\nbe joking.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_020: All acting. Honestly, I'm quick to fright. But there\nisn't really a choice.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_021: Wait. You're a scaredy-cat, but you play a scary role?
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_022: Yeah. Makeup on my face, a mask on my heart,\nand I become the clown.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_023: With my real, scaredy-cat self buried waaay below\nthe surface.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_024: You wear a mask to hide the fear in your heart. Do\nyou think I could do that for my fear, Mr....Jester?
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_025: Maybe... I'm not recommending it. The fear doesn't\nreally go away—you're just pushing it down.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_026: Works for me. Even a little effort is worth it if it\nhelps me not be scared.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_027: Maybe I could be like an Apprentice Jester? But only\nif you try not to scare me so much.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_028: Hehe. More moderate scaring—got it. I don't need\nanything in return, but please do promise me this.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_029: You can't tell anyone my secret. OK?
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_030: Of course. I promise.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_031: Well then, Peter! Let's play again soon. I had so\nmuch fun makin' you squirm! Heh heh HEH!
MID_SE_Pet_Max_C_032: It's definitely just an act...right?
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_001: Peter! On your right!
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_002: Ah! Enemies! Not while I'm here!
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_025: 
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_003: Thanks, Maxim. I appreciate the help.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_004: I was so focused on the distant enemies, I didn't even\nnotice the ones nearby. That was close.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_005: You kept a cool head even as the enemy advanced.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_006: The Peter I knew a few years ago was terrified of\neverything—including me.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_007: Well, if we're talking about the way things were\nyears ago, let's talk about your makeover, Maxim.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_008: I'm still getting used to not seeing all that caked-on\nmakeup. It's hard to think you were so scary once.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_009: It's nice to hear you say that. Like I told you before—\nI'm nothing like Jester.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_010: I'm so timid that just thinking about blood makes\nme kinda dizzy.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_011: It took work to play him. The voice, the unsettling\nlaugh—I practiced those for hours a day.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_012: I even had people tell me gruesome stories to shore\nup my tolerance for violence.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_013: Which led to the, ah, odd fainting spell, or getting\nlaid up in bed all day. Embarrassing, I know.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_014: I'd have been too scared to even practice a role\nlike that.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_015: But you shouldn't be embarrassed. I respect you for\nit, Maxim.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_016: Hehe. Thanks. I respect what you've done too.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_017: You were terrified of me at first, but you got more\ncomfortable eventually.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_018: Sure. Over time, yeah.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_019: And somehow a lot fewer things scare me now.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_020: And a lot of that is because of your training, Maxim.\nOr should I say Jester?
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_021: Ha. I'll let the Infernal Clown know you said thanks.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_022: Hehe. Hey, if I ever have a kid who's a scaredy-cat,\nat least I've got a good plan to cope with it.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_023: I'll just slosh on some Jester makeup and help them\nconquer their fears.
MID_SE_Pet_Max_B_024: Oh, I think that's— I would not recommend that.